<p>US Vice President JD Vance is visiting Budapest on Tuesday to meet Prime Minister Viktor Orbán and appear at a campaign event just days before Hungary’s parliamentary election on Sunday. The trip is the clearest sign yet that the Trump administration is willing to openly back Orbán as the Hungarian leader faces what several outlets describe as his toughest electoral test in years. With the vote only five days away, Vance’s visit gives Orbán a high-level show of support in the campaign’s final stretch.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/MSVdzZ8HGcQhmWye-pEuwMNRwTYc9JAqIBGync4aXMjVr-fe1H9OI58kTK4YEr8soGJPowHZff3dLkvz1w7ClJ-HLQCGSIk6wi9lVE1osTlcrtGanHUN2enM4KRXAHW8g3Fd8T3kmbqGxRpKfFYGWcBsJOPgDO89fkCEOO9ITeCMA1FemYM8Bq7EPaiiL-yPi5hekGXl' alt='Prime Minister Viktor Orban at a campaign rally in Kaposvar, Hungary, in March.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Campaign staging: Politico reported that Orbán plans to use Vance’s visit for a Budapest press conference and a flag-waving rally at a 24,000-seat football stadium.</li><li>Limited lift so far: Earlier endorsements from President Trump and Secretary of State Marco Rubio have not reversed Orbán’s flagging fortunes, Politico said, making Vance’s trip a late gamble.</li><li>US stake: The New York Times said Vance’s visit shows that Russia is not the only outside power invested in the election’s outcome, underscoring the vote’s strategic importance.</li><li>Ally branding: Politico said Orbán sees the visit as a chance to present himself as the Trump administration’s leading European ally.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Hungarian government: Officials describe the visit as proof of exceptionally close ties between Budapest and the Trump White House, and as political validation for Orbán ahead of the vote. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-vice-president-vance-visits-hungary-to-boost-orban/article70832986.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>European analysts: Coverage in Europe frames the trip less as routine diplomacy and more as evidence of ideological alignment between Orbán and the US far right. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/7/vance-heads-to-budapest-to-shore-up-orbans-support-before-sunday-vote'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>EU observers: Financial Times coverage treats Hungary’s election as a broader test of nationalist politics inside the bloc, making Vance’s appearance relevant beyond Hungary’s domestic politics. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/a528c2fe-c448-4ebf-abbf-3d744d9004c4'>Financial Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/a528c2fe-c448-4ebf-abbf-3d744d9004c4'>JD Vance jets into Hungary to boost Orbán in final week of election race</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/07/world/europe/vance-hungary-orban-fidesz-election.html'>Vance to Visit Hungary to Boost Orban Before Election</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-vice-president-vance-hungary-visit-viktor-orban/article70832986.ece'>U.S. Vice President Vance visits Hungary to boost Orban ahead of pivotal election</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/7/vance-heads-to-budapest-to-shore-up-orbans-support-before-sunday-vote'>Vance heads to Budapest to shore up Orban’s support before Sunday vote</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/vice-president-vance-visits-hungary-to-boost-orban-ahead-of-pivotal-election'>Vice President Vance visits Hungary to boost Orban ahead of pivotal election</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cyv16lq2rp1o'>JD Vance due in Hungary to back Orban&#x27;s re-election bid</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/podcast/berlin-playbook-podcast/wahlhilfe-fur-orban-vance-in-budapest/'>Wahlhilfe für Orbán: Vance in Budapest</a> - politico.eu</li></ul>